<article class="env-corollary" id="05DX">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05DX">Corollary <span data-tag="05DX">5.1.5.18</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be right fibration of $\infty $-categories and let $n$ be an integer. Then $U$ is $n$-faithful if and only if, for every object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the Kan complex $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C}$ is $(n-1)$-truncated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      For $n \geq 0$, the result follows by combining Variant <a data-tag="05DW" href="/tag/05DW">5.1.5.17</a> with Example <a data-tag="0587" href="/tag/0587">4.7.6.10</a>. We may therefore assume without loss of generality that $n &lt; 0$. In this case, we wish to show that $U$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories if and only if every fiber $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C}$ is a contractible Kan complex (see Examples <a data-tag="05AY" href="/tag/05AY">4.8.3.13</a> and <a data-tag="054R" href="/tag/054R">3.5.7.3</a>). In fact, both conditions are equivalent to the requirement that $U$ is a trivial Kan fibration: see Propositions <a data-tag="01NU" href="/tag/01NU">4.4.2.14</a> and <a data-tag="01G7" href="/tag/01G7">4.5.6.20</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
